## 10. Key Takeaways 🧠

- Intersection means common elements.
- HashSet stores unique elements.
- `add()` inserts an element.
- `contains()` checks whether an element exists.
- Two HashSets help separate stored elements and common elements.
- Enhanced for loop can traverse a collection.
- Convert HashSet into an array when an array is required as output.

